<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlanthus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλανθος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A</i>
			
			<i>river in Sarmatia</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4,
				10, 54</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the seamen whom Bacchus changed into
			dolphins</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3, 617</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The father of the Athenian king Codrus</i>, <i><span class="en">Vell. 1, 2,
				1</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlanthēus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrisyl.</span></b> ), a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to a Melanthus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					625</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
